{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01R4T4fTWN9UP8QMtvtPkoMh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DVjSuExduGkSWtUUfLNTL4","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"Explore","description":"Find architectural friction in almanac codebase","prompt":"Explore the almanac codebase at /Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac to find architectural friction worth fixing in a single sitting (not deep refactors, but the kind of cleanup a careful maintainer would do).\n\nContext: this is round 3 of an autonomous improvement loop. Rounds 1-2 already addressed major issues (slug unification, worker-status record extraction). The CONTEXT.md describes the intended architecture — your job is to find places the code drifts from it.\n\nSpecifically look for:\n\n1. **Shallow modules** — files in `lib/` where the interface is nearly as complex as the implementation. Apply the deletion test: would deleting concentrate complexity, or just move it?\n\n2. **CLAUDE.md violations** the team flagged as \"existing offenders to NOT pattern-match from\":\n   - `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/...` paths in skills (should be `~/.claude/skills/almanac/<name>/scripts/...`)\n   - Raw `echo` errors in `cmd/*.sh` (should use `_die`/`_info`/`_error` from `lib/core.sh`)\n   - Listed offenders: `codebase-improve`, `diagnose`, `tdd`, `task-start`, `grill-me`, `agents-md-audit`, `ralph-loop`, `cmd/list.sh`, `cmd/sync.sh`\n\n3. **Inconsistencies between similar files** — e.g. one provider adapter does X, another does Y for no reason. One loop adapter handles a case its sibling doesn't.\n\n4. **Dead code / unreferenced helpers** — functions in `lib/*.sh` that no callsite uses anymore (post-refactor leftovers from rounds 1-2).\n\n5. **Test gaps** — recently-extracted modules without test coverage (worker-status record, slug function).\n\n6. **Documentation drift** — README.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/CONTRIBUTING.md vs actual file layout/skill list/CLI commands.\n\nWalk the tree: `ls lib/`, `ls cmd/`, `ls skills/*/`, `ls tests/`. Read CLAUDE.md, README.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md. Read each lib/*.sh briefly. Sample 3-4 skills' SKILL.md.\n\nReport a punch list of 5-12 concrete findings, each with:\n- File:line where the issue lives\n- One-sentence problem statement\n- Whether it's a 1-line fix, a small refactor (10-50 LOC), or a bigger change\n- Whether tests need updating\n\nSkip findings that would require user judgment calls. Skip findings that would invent new abstractions. Focus on cleanup that's clearly correct.\n\nReport under 600 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4667,"cache_read_input_tokens":36506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4667},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"250917c1-763a-4661-b412-670ee21b67f2","uuid":"2302595c-8e0f-4f24-bfde-52ce9065d390","request_id":"req_011CbRKjx9UkJigjFqeBCzRW"}
