{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BQAqcqooMdtgAXJA1tMUri","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Almanac\n2\t\n3\tPersonal agent toolkit — curated skills for LLM coding agents.\n4\t\n5\tSkills follow the [Agent Skills Open Standard](https://agentskills.io/specification) and work across Claude Code, OpenCode, Cursor, Codex, and [25+ compatible agents](https://agentskills.io).\n6\t\n7\t## What are skills?\n8\t\n9\tSkills are portable instruction sets that teach coding agents *how* to do things — commit code, create PRs, run TDD, fix CI, and more. Each skill is a single Markdown file (`SKILL.md`) with YAML frontmatter. Agents discover and load them automatically.\n10\t\n11\tRun any skill as a slash command in your agent (e.g. `/commit`, `/ship`, `/ralph-loop`, `/harden-loop`, `/converge-loop`).\n12\t\n13\tSkills are organized by category in the repo (`skills/git/`, `skills/productivity/`, `skills/other/`, …) and flattened at install time so Claude Code's flat skill discovery finds them.\n14\t\n15\t### Skill highlights\n16\t\n17\t| Skill | Use |\n18\t|-------|-----|\n19\t| `ralph-loop` | Build a PRD slice queue task-by-task, with each iteration committed. |\n20\t| `harden-loop` | Harden one target through reviewers, ratification, fixer, and feedback gates. |\n21\t| `converge-loop` | Repeat one custom exec command toward a mutable `goal.md` until an overseer says done. |\n22\t\n23\t## Install\n24\t\n25\t```bash\n26\t# One-time setup — clones to ~/.almanac and adds to PATH\n27\tbash install.sh\n28\t\n29\t# Pick your agent\n30\talmanac install claude-code\n31\t```\n32\t\n33\t<details>\n34\t<summary>Other agents</summary>\n35\t\n36\t```bash\n37\talmanac install opencode\n38\talmanac install cursor\n39\talmanac install codex\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\t`almanac install codex` links skills into `~/.agents/skills/almanac/<name>`, so skills can be invoked as `$ship`, `$commit`, etc. or browsed from `/skills` after restarting Codex.\n43\t\n44\tOr manually symlink:\n45\t\n46\t```bash\n47\tln -s ~/.almanac/skills ~/.config/opencode/skills/almanac   # OpenCode\n48\tln -s ~/.almanac/skills ~/.cursor/skills/almanac             # Cursor\n49\tln -s ~/.almanac/skills ~/.agents/skills/almanac             # Codex\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\t</details>\n53\t\n54\t### Global config\n55\t\n56\tThe installer symlinks a versioned global instruction file into each provider, all pointing at the same canonical source (`providers/_shared/AGENTS.md`):\n57\t\n58\t- `claude-code` → `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`\n59\t- `codex` → `~/.codex/AGENTS.md`\n60\t\n61\t```bash\n62\talmanac install claude-code                  # skips if you have a custom CLAUDE.md\n63\talmanac install claude-code --global-config  # replaces with almanac's version\n64\talmanac install codex                        # same, for ~/.codex/AGENTS.md\n65\t```\n66\t\n67\t## CLI\n68\t\n69\t```\n70\talmanac                      Open the interactive loop hub (in a TTY); else print help\n71\talmanac hub                  Open the interactive loop hub (launch / list / watch loops)\n72\talmanac hub --new <type>     Launch a new ralph|harden run (add --dry-run to preview)\n73\talmanac install <provider>   Install for a provider\n74\talmanac uninstall <provider> Remove from a provider\n75\talmanac list                 List available providers and install status\n76\talmanac ralph                Launch the interactive Ralph loop CLI\n77\talmanac harden <target>      Fan out read-only reviewers (one per lens) and aggregate findings\n78\t                             (lens set via HARDEN_LENSES; default: correctness security perf edge-cases contracts)\n79\talmanac harden <target> --goal \"<goal>\"\n80\t                             Draft a harden-loop rubric for a target\n81\talmanac harden <target> --approve\n82\t                             Approve an edited harden-loop rubric\n83\talmanac harden <target> --fix\n84\t                             Run one sequential fixer over open blocking findings + feedback loops\n85\talmanac harden <target> --loop [--rounds N]\n86\t                             Run the convergence loop until converged or budget hit\n87\t                             (HITL checkpoint each round: ship / continue / steer)\n88\talmanac harden <target> --watch\n89\t                             Redraw the live supervision dashboard for the latest run\n90\talmanac harden <target> --watch-worker <lens>\n91\t                             Stream one reviewer's live event log\n92\talmanac converge --goal \"<goal>\" --exec \"<cmd>\" [--rounds N]\n93\t                             Run a generic convergence loop with one custom exec per round\n94\talmanac converge <slug>      Print a converge run status summary\n95\talmanac converge <slug> --watch\n96\t                             Redraw the live converge dashboard\n97\talmanac converge <slug> --stop\n98\t                             Request a graceful stop at the next round boundary\n99\talmanac update               Update almanac (git pull + re-install)\n100\talmanac sync                 Check adapted skills for upstream changes\n101\talmanac doctor               Report optional-dependency status (gum, gh, jq)\n102\talmanac help                 Show help\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\t### Loop examples\n106\t\n107\t```bash\n108\talmanac ralph\n109\talmanac harden lib/role.sh --loop --rounds 3\n110\talmanac converge \\\n111\t  --goal \"Improve the codebase until no major architecture friction remains\" \\\n112\t  --exec \"claude -p '/almanac:codebase-improve'\" \\\n113\t  --rounds 5\n114\t```\n115\t\n116\t### Repository structure\n117\t\n118\t```text\n119\tbin/almanac\n120\tcmd/\n121\t  converge.sh\n122\t  harden.sh\n123\t  ralph.sh\n124\tlib/\n125\t  converge-core.sh\n126\t  harden-core.sh\n127\t  loop-launcher.sh\n128\t  loops/\n129\t    converge.sh\n130\t    harden.sh\n131\t    ralph.sh\n132\tskills/\n133\t  loop/\n134\t    converge-loop/\n135\t      SKILL.md\n136\t    harden-loop/\n137\t      SKILL.md\n138\t    ralph-loop/\n139\t      SKILL.md\n140\t```\n141\t\n142\t### Upstream sync\n143\t\n144\tSeven skills are adapted from upstream repositories:\n145\t\n146\t| Skill | Upstream |\n147\t|-------|----------|\n148\t| codebase-improve | [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) |\n149\t| diagnose | [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) |\n150\t| grill-me | [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) |\n151\t| grill-plan | [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) |\n152\t| issues-create | [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) |\n153\t| prd-create | [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) |\n154\t| tdd | [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) |\n155\t\n156\tRun `almanac sync` to check for updates.\n157\t\n158\t## Adding a skill\n159\t\n160\t1. Create `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter\n161\t2. Use `noun-verb` naming (e.g. `pr-create`, `ci-fix`) — lowercase, hyphens only\n162\t3. Description starts with \"Use when...\"\n163\t4. Run `bash tests/test-skills.sh` to validate\n164\t\n165\tSee [docs/CONTRIBUTING.md](docs/CONTRIBUTING.md) for the full guide.\n166\t\n167\t## License\n168\t\n169\tMIT\n170\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVjSuExduGkSWtUUfLNTL4","session_id":"250917c1-763a-4661-b412-670ee21b67f2","uuid":"cf2520b3-2bf6-4029-8693-2a52327bceee","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:18:02.926Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find architectural friction in almanac codebase"}
