{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Unz1oLmYBs4259edeAq3ac","type":"tool_result","content":"13-\n14-## Glossary\n15-\n16:Use these terms exactly in every suggestion. Consistent language is the point — don't drift into \"component,\" \"service,\" \"API,\" or \"boundary.\" Full definitions in `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/LANGUAGE.md`.\n17-\n18-- **Module** — anything with an interface and an implementation (function, class, package, slice).\n19-- **Interface** — everything a caller must know to use the module: types, invariants, error modes, ordering, config. Not just the type signature.\n--\n24-- **Leverage** — what callers get from depth.\n25-- **Locality** — what maintainers get from depth: change, bugs, knowledge concentrated in one place.\n26-\n27:Key principles (see `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/LANGUAGE.md` for the full list):\n28-\n29-- **Deletion test**: imagine deleting the module. If complexity vanishes, it was a pass-through. If complexity reappears across N callers, it was earning its keep.\n30-- **The interface is the test surface.**\n--\n62-- **Solution** — plain English description of what would change\n63-- **Benefits** — explained in terms of locality and leverage, and also in how tests would improve\n64-\n65:**Use CONTEXT.md vocabulary for the domain, and `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/LANGUAGE.md` vocabulary for the architecture.**\n66-\n67-**ADR conflicts**: if a candidate contradicts an existing ADR, only surface it when the friction is real enough to warrant revisiting the ADR. Mark it clearly (e.g. _\"contradicts ADR-0007 — but worth reopening because…\"_).\n68-\n--\n77-- **Naming a deepened module after a concept not in `CONTEXT.md`?** Add the term to `CONTEXT.md`. Create the file lazily if it doesn't exist.\n78-- **Sharpening a fuzzy term during the conversation?** Update `CONTEXT.md` right there.\n79-- **User rejects the candidate with a load-bearing reason?** Offer an ADR so future reviews don't re-suggest it. Only offer when the reason would actually be needed by a future explorer.\n80:- **Want to explore alternative interfaces for the deepened module?** See `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/INTERFACE-DESIGN.md`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVjSuExduGkSWtUUfLNTL4","session_id":"250917c1-763a-4661-b412-670ee21b67f2","uuid":"43d924cd-7acc-4abd-97ee-c949f491a44f","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:18:11.742Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find architectural friction in almanac codebase"}
