est-run.sh, test-ralph-run-registry.sh)\n- Fix: Add unit test to `tests/test-run.sh` covering edge cases (special chars, length, idempotence) (~15 LOC)\n- Tests: Needed\n\n**5. Test gap: `lib/run.sh` TSV record functions lack unit coverage for worker-status schema**\n- File: `lib/run.sh:134` (`almanac_loop_tsv_record_set`, `almanac_loop_worker_record_fields`)\n- Problem: Worker-status record engine (extracted from loop-core.sh round 2) passes integration tests but lacks isolated schema unit tests\n- Fix: Add to `tests/test-run.sh` covering set/get-by-name, field initialization, and round-trip (inline with slug test above, ~20 LOC)\n- Tests: Needed\n\n**6. Docs stale: README.md skill count and category list**\n- File: `/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/README.md:19` (highlights only git/loop/other, misses comms/agents-md/productivity)\n- Problem: README highlights only three categories; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md correctly lists five\n- Fix: Update README skill-highlights table to include comms/, agents-md/, productivity/ examples (1-line addition to intro)\n- Tests: None needed\n\n**7. `loop-launcher.sh` shadows `_info` function from core.sh without dependency declaration**\n- File: `/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/lib/loop-launcher.sh:1–50`\n- Problem: Uses `_info`, `_error`, `_success` but does not source `lib/core.sh` (relies on caller sourcing it first)\n- Fix: Add `source \"$ALMANAC_HOME/lib/core.sh\"` at top, document implicit dependency in CONTEXT.md module-map comment (~1 line)\n- Tests: None needed (integration tests already cover this implicitly)\n\n**8. Provider adapters inconsistency: no abstract contract test**\n- File: `lib/providers/{codex,claude}.sh`\n- Problem: Both adapters must implement the same 7-function contract but there's no test pinning the interface (test-providers.sh only samples behavior)\n- Fix: Add unit test skeleton in `tests/test-providers.sh` checking both adapters have all verbs (grep for function names,