{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ea6n32XRjtKYLTGVmfSawg","type":"tool_result","content":"30\t2. **Curl / HTTP script** against a running dev server.\n31\t3. **CLI invocation** with fixture input, diffing stdout against known-good snapshot.\n32\t4. **Headless browser script** (Playwright / Puppeteer) — drives UI, asserts on DOM/console/network.\n33\t5. **Replay a captured trace.** Save a real network request / payload / event log to disk; replay through code path in isolation.\n34\t6. **Throwaway harness.** Spin up minimal subset of system (one service, mocked deps) that exercises bug code path with single fn call.\n35\t7. **Property / fuzz loop.** If bug is \"sometimes wrong output\", run 1000 random inputs and look for failure mode.\n36\t8. **Bisection harness.** If bug appeared between two known states (commit, dataset, version), automate \"boot at state X, check, repeat\" so you can `git bisect run` it.\n37\t9. **Differential loop.** Run same input through old-version vs new-version (or two configs) and diff outputs.\n38\t10. **HITL bash script.** Last resort. If human must click, drive _them_ with `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/hitl-loop.template.sh` so loop is still structured. Captured output feeds back to you.\n39\t\n40\tBuild the right feedback loop → bug is 90% fixed.\n41\t\n42\t### Iterate on the loop itself\n43\t\n44\tTreat loop as product. Once you have _a_ loop, ask:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"250917c1-763a-4661-b412-670ee21b67f2","uuid":"ded1012a-171b-49e9-9985-1d70e6c9370c","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:20:19.611Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/skills/other/diagnose/SKILL.md","content":"2. **Curl / HTTP script** against a running dev server.\n3. **CLI invocation** with fixture input, diffing stdout against known-good snapshot.\n4. **Headless browser script** (Playwright / Puppeteer) — drives UI, asserts on DOM/console/network.\n5. **Replay a captured trace.** Save a real network request / payload / event log to disk; replay through code path in isolation.\n6. **Throwaway harness.** Spin up minimal subset of system (one service, mocked deps) that exercises bug code path with single fn call.\n7. **Property / fuzz loop.** If bug is \"sometimes wrong output\", run 1000 random inputs and look for failure mode.\n8. **Bisection harness.** If bug appeared between two known states (commit, dataset, version), automate \"boot at state X, check, repeat\" so you can `git bisect run` it.\n9. **Differential loop.** Run same input through old-version vs new-version (or two configs) and diff outputs.\n10. **HITL bash script.** Last resort. If human must click, drive _them_ with `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/hitl-loop.template.sh` so loop is still structured. Captured output feeds back to you.\n\nBuild the right feedback loop → bug is 90% fixed.\n\n### Iterate on the loop itself\n\nTreat loop as product. Once you have _a_ loop, ask:","numLines":15,"startLine":30,"totalLines":127}}}
